Name: scrollbarBackColor

Type: property

Syntax: set the scrollbarBackColor of {<field> | <scrollbar> | <group>} to {<colorName> | <RGBColor> | empty}

Summary:
Specifies the color used to draw the track of a <field|field's>,
<scrollbar|scrollbar's>, or <group|group's> scrollbar.

Associations: field, scrollbar, group

Introduced: 1.0.0

OS: mac, windows, linux

Platforms: desktop

Example:
set the scrollbarBackColor of field 1 to "200,200,200"

Example:
set the scrollbarBackColor of field "myField" to "#E0E0E0"

Example:
set the scrollbarBackColor of scrollbar 1 to white

Example:
set the scrollbarBackColor of group "sidebar" to "240,240,240"

Example:
-- Restore native scrollbar appearance
set the scrollbarBackColor of field 1 to empty

Value:
The <scrollbarBackColor> is a <color reference>.
The <colorName> is any standard color name.

The <RGBColor> consists of three comma-separated <integer|integers>
between zero and 255, specifying the level of each of red, green, and
blue; or an HTML-style color consisting of a hash mark (#) followed by
three <hexadecimal> numbers, one for each of red, green, and blue.

By default, the <scrollbarBackColor> of a <field>, <scrollbar>, or
<group> is empty.

Description:
Use the <scrollbarBackColor> property to color the track (the channel
the thumb slides along) of a scrollbar. When this property or
<scrollbarForeColor> is set to a non-empty value, the engine draws the
scrollbar entirely in software using the specified colors, bypassing the
platform's native scrollbar renderer.

If the <scrollbarBackColor> is empty but <scrollbarForeColor> is set,
the track is drawn in gray.

Setting the <scrollbarBackColor> to empty restores the scrollbar to its
native platform appearance, provided <scrollbarForeColor> is also empty.

For a <scrollbar> control, the property is stored directly on the
control. For a <field> or <group>, the property is stored on the object
and applied to the scrollbar it owns.

>*Cross-platform note:* On Mac OS, the native scrollbar is rendered by
> the system theme and cannot be tinted through standard color properties.
> Setting <scrollbarBackColor> or <scrollbarForeColor> causes the scrollbar
> to be drawn in software, which applies the color reliably across all
> platforms.

References: color reference (glossary), integer (glossary),
hexadecimal (glossary), field (object), scrollbar (object),
group (object), scrollbarForeColor (property), scrollbarWidth (property),
backColor (property), vScrollbar (property), hScrollbar (property)

Tags: ui
